{# The view counter goes up on every visit, this one included, so no stored copy of this page
   can match the next render. The crawl reads the word random here and compares it with the
   digits masked instead, which still checks the page around the count. #}
<p>This page tracks how many times it has been viewed.</p>

<h2>Total Page Views</h2>

<div class="counter">
  {$totalCount}
</div>

<h2>Statistics</h2>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Metric</th>
    <th>Value</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Total Views (all time)</td>
    <td><strong>{$totalCount}</strong></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Views Today</td>
    <td><strong>{$todayCount}</strong></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Current Date</td>
    <td>{$currentDate}</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p style="color: #999; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 20px;">
  The counter increments each time this page is loaded. Daily counts reset at midnight.
</p>